{"id":"199139c5a60bcfcc","group":"58","path":"58/batch02/58-df-totally-bounded.md","title":"Totally Bounded","display":"df-totally-bounded — Totally Bounded","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-totally-bounded","aliases":["58-df-totally-bounded","Totally Bounded"],"display":"df-totally-bounded — Totally Bounded","depends_on":["[[../batch16/58-df-metric-space.md]]","[[../batch16/58-df-omega.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-totally-bounded"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-totally-bounded</span><span>Totally Bounded</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-totally-bounded — Totally Bounded"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"ce876585d129ce97\" href=\"?note=ce876585d129ce97\" title=\"../batch16/58-df-metric-space.md\">../batch16/58-df-metric-space.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"5045d216c83e75cb\" href=\"?note=5045d216c83e75cb\" title=\"../batch16/58-df-omega.md\">../batch16/58-df-omega.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{MetricSpace}_S(X,d)\">\\(\\mathrm{MetricSpace}_S(X,d)\\)</span>（see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"ce876585d129ce97\" href=\"?note=ce876585d129ce97\" title=\"../batch16/58-df-metric-space.md\">../batch16/58-df-metric-space.md</a>）</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"E\\subseteq X\">\\(E\\subseteq X\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"B_d(x,\\epsilon)\\coloneqq\\{y\\in X\\mid d(x,y)&lt;\\epsilon\\}\">\\(B_d(x,\\epsilon)\\coloneqq\\{y\\in X\\mid d(x,y)&lt;\\epsilon\\}\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{TotallyBounded}_S(E,X,d)\">\\(\\mathrm{TotallyBounded}_S(E,X,d)\\)</span>（本文件定义的全有界谓词）</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}totally\\text{-}bounded} \\vdash \\mathrm{TotallyBounded}_S(E,X,d)\\leftrightarrow\\left(\\mathrm{MetricSpace}_S(X,d)\\land E\\subseteq X\\land\\forall\\epsilon\\in\\mathbb R_{&gt;0}\\;\\exists N\\subseteq X\\;\\left(|N|&lt;\\omega\\land E\\subseteq\\bigcup_{x\\in N}B_d(x,\\epsilon)\\right)\\right)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}totally\\text{-}bounded} \\vdash \\mathrm{TotallyBounded}_S(E,X,d)\\leftrightarrow\\left(\\mathrm{MetricSpace}_S(X,d)\\land E\\subseteq X\\land\\forall\\epsilon\\in\\mathbb R_{&gt;0}\\;\\exists N\\subseteq X\\;\\left(|N|&lt;\\omega\\land E\\subseteq\\bigcup_{x\\in N}B_d(x,\\epsilon)\\right)\\right)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Totally bounded: finite covers by arbitrarily small balls; no infinite &quot;spread&quot;</li>\n<li>在度量空间中，紧致等价于完备且全有界。</li>\n<li>Finite dimension: in <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb{R}^n\">\\(\\mathbb{R}^n\\)</span>, totally bounded <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\iff\">\\(\\iff\\)</span> bounded; infinite dimension needed</li>\n<li>Riesz lemma: shows infinite-dimensional normed spaces not locally compact</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Reference\">[Reference]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Munkres, Topology</li>\n<li>Kadison and Ringrose, Fundamentals of the Theory of Operator Algebras</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2},{"id":"Reference","text":"[Reference]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch16/58-df-metric-space.md","status":"resolved","id":"ce876585d129ce97","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch16/58-df-metric-space.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch16/58-df-omega.md","status":"resolved","id":"5045d216c83e75cb","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch16/58-df-omega.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch16/58-df-metric-space.md","status":"resolved","id":"ce876585d129ce97","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{MetricSpace}_S(X,d)$（see [[../batch16/58-df-metric-space.md]]）","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"\\mathrm{MetricSpace}_S(X,d)","display":false},{"tex":"E\\subseteq X","display":false},{"tex":"B_d(x,\\epsilon)\\coloneqq\\{y\\in X\\mid d(x,y)<\\epsilon\\}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{TotallyBounded}_S(E,X,d)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}totally\\text{-}bounded} \\vdash \\mathrm{TotallyBounded}_S(E,X,d)\\leftrightarrow\\left(\\mathrm{MetricSpace}_S(X,d)\\land E\\subseteq X\\land\\forall\\epsilon\\in\\mathbb R_{>0}\\;\\exists N\\subseteq X\\;\\left(|N|<\\omega\\land E\\subseteq\\bigcup_{x\\in N}B_d(x,\\epsilon)\\right)\\right)","display":true},{"tex":"\\mathbb{R}^n","display":false},{"tex":"\\iff","display":false}],"bytes":1347,"backlinks":[{"id":"ec17b877f67b9c76","anchor":"ref-2","locations":["元数据 · depends_on","正文"],"count":2,"excerpt":"$\\mathrm{TotallyBounded}_S:V^3\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}$ (from [[../batch02/58-df-totally-bounded.md]])."},{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-1308","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch02/58-df-totally-bounded.md|58-df-totally-bounded]]（batch02）"}],"outgoing":["ce876585d129ce97","5045d216c83e75cb"]}